          <declname>min_size</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Allocate a buffer, reusing the given one if large enough. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Contrary to <ref refid="group__lavu__mem__funcs_1ga0e8e75b89c5fa2966b8fbffbdb6ec774" kindref="member">av_fast_realloc()</ref>, the current buffer contents might not be preserved and on error the old buffer is freed, thus no special handling to avoid memleaks is necessary.</para>
<para><computeroutput>*ptr</computeroutput> is allowed to be <computeroutput>NULL</computeroutput>, in which case allocation always happens if <computeroutput>size_needed</computeroutput> is greater than 0.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="normal">uint8_t<sp/>*buf<sp/>=<sp/>...;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="group__lavu__mem__funcs_1ga29d0252b981f157e713a68ffca52f003" kindref="member">av_fast_malloc</ref>(&amp;buf,<sp/>&amp;current_size,<sp/>size_needed);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(!buf)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Allocation<sp/>failed;<sp/>buf<sp/>already<sp/>freed</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/><ref refid="group__lavu__error_1gae4bb6f165973d09584e0ec0f335f69ca" kindref="member">AVERROR</ref>(ENOMEM);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
